WEBVTT

00:03.680 --> 00:05.280
So now let's have a quick recap.

00:05.280 --> 00:11.840
So we have learned that the CTE the common table expression is a temporary named result, like a virtual

00:11.880 --> 00:14.840
table that could be used from different places in the query.

00:14.840 --> 00:17.040
And we have a lot of advantages for the CTE.

00:17.280 --> 00:23.960
The main one is it breaks the complexity of query into small multiple pieces, which makes our query

00:24.000 --> 00:28.480
much easier to read and as well to understand, so it improves readability.

00:28.520 --> 00:34.240
Another advantage of the city is that those small multiple pieces, they are really easy to manage and

00:34.240 --> 00:35.080
to develop.

00:35.080 --> 00:40.080
So those pieces are like self-contained which makes our queries more modular.

00:40.080 --> 00:43.440
So it introduces modularity inside our queries.

00:43.440 --> 00:49.640
And we also learned that the CTE help us to reduce the redundancy inside our queries, where it makes

00:49.640 --> 00:54.840
the results of one query usable in multiple places inside our query.

00:54.840 --> 00:57.880
So it makes our code smaller and reduce redundancy.

00:57.880 --> 01:05.000
And one more advantage of the city is that it helps us to do looping and iterating in SQL by using the

01:05.000 --> 01:06.000
recursive CTE.

01:06.200 --> 01:12.010
And we have understood as well that we can treat the CTE results as any other physical table inside

01:12.010 --> 01:15.690
our database so we can treat it and handle it like any other tables.

01:15.690 --> 01:23.210
Only one exception that this table lives only in one query, so we cannot query the CTE from an external

01:23.370 --> 01:24.010
query.

01:24.050 --> 01:28.370
Now we have learned that the result of the CTE could be used from the main query.

01:28.370 --> 01:34.370
This is the classical one, but not only we can use it in the main query, but also we can use it in

01:34.570 --> 01:38.690
another city query which leads to having nested cities.

01:38.730 --> 01:44.770
And of course we have learned as well we can use the result of the CTE within itself, which makes the

01:44.770 --> 01:48.410
CTE recursive and allows for looping and iterating.

01:48.410 --> 01:53.570
And I can only keep recommending to not use more than five cities in one query.

01:53.610 --> 01:58.970
Otherwise you're going to get the exact opposite and benefits from cities where your code can be really

01:58.970 --> 02:01.570
hard to understand and to read, and even to extend.

02:01.610 --> 02:02.290
Okay my friends.

02:02.290 --> 02:06.170
So with that, you have covered this amazing and very important technique in SQL.

02:06.210 --> 02:08.530
The common table expressions, the CTE.

02:08.570 --> 02:13.530
Now in the next step we're going to talk about a new type of objects that you can use in databases.

02:13.530 --> 02:15.410
We don't have only tables we have as well.

02:15.450 --> 02:20.970
Views and views are amazing in order to give you dynamic and flexibility in your project.

02:20.970 --> 02:22.370
So let's talk about views.
